{"results": [{"id": "hp_doc_58fc84fbfc07a9ffc608ab08aac1bff2b59f8c2c51fbf86e27bf063beb60e32d", "title": "Damien Bay", "text": "Damien Bay ( ) is located north-northeast of Hamilton Bay on the southeast coast of South Georgia. It was named after the yacht \"Damien II\", owned by Sally and Jerome Poncet, residents of Beaver Island in the Falkland Islands. The Poncets conducted investigations of the breeding colonies of seals and seabirds around the coastline of South Georgia. The \"Damien II\" was chartered by the British Antarctic Survey for various wildlife surveys between 1985 and 1992.", "score": 22.988}, {"id": "hp_doc_c59416d241acb4bbb477c4eb5465d4ee2a8bfc510df608693dc1e962d53ba53a", "title": "Sally Prouty", "text": "Sally Prouty (born Sarah Green) (December 23, 1922 - September 7, 2014) was an American retired table tennis champion. She was inducted into the United States of America Table Tennis (USATT) Hall of Fame in 1979.", "score": 10.7141}, {"id": "hp_doc_e21331edaf7c68662d77deb88331781fadb0964066b4b9c427cf46a92859a929", "title": "Sally, Irene and Mary (1938 film)", "text": "Sally, Irene and Mary is a 1938 American comedy film directed by William A. Seiter and written by Harry Tugend and Jack Yellen. The film stars Alice Faye, Tony Martin, Fred Allen, Joan Davis, Marjorie Weaver and Gregory Ratoff. The film was released on March 4, 1938, by 20th Century Fox.", "score": 9.8805}], "remaining_searches": 2}
