{"results": [{"id": "hp_doc_b24953f44a17894b07efdade3ed0e5fdc643a9426400354455efb9e8b7070bbb", "title": "Falkland Islands", "text": "The Falkland Islands ( ; Spanish: \"Islas Malvinas\" , ] ) are an archipelago in the South Atlantic Ocean on the Patagonian Shelf. The principal islands are about 300 mi east of South America's southern Patagonian coast, at a latitude of about 52°S. The archipelago, with an area of 4700 sqmi , comprises East Falkland, West Falkland and 776 smaller islands. As a British overseas territory, the Falklands have internal self-governance, and the United Kingdom takes responsibility for their defence and foreign affairs. The islands' capital is Stanley on East Falkland.", "score": 37.8947}, {"id": "hp_doc_58fc84fbfc07a9ffc608ab08aac1bff2b59f8c2c51fbf86e27bf063beb60e32d", "title": "Damien Bay", "text": "Damien Bay ( ) is located north-northeast of Hamilton Bay on the southeast coast of South Georgia. It was named after the yacht \"Damien II\", owned by Sally and Jerome Poncet, residents of Beaver Island in the Falkland Islands. The Poncets conducted investigations of the breeding colonies of seals and seabirds around the coastline of South Georgia. The \"Damien II\" was chartered by the British Antarctic Survey for various wildlife surveys between 1985 and 1992.", "score": 18.691}, {"id": "hp_doc_7cacc3171c8a2d58553114d9fd2fdb5ee2c6d39a50079ebc21d5f17d4c86d96e", "title": "Southern Patagonian Ice Field", "text": "The Southern Patagonian Ice Field (Spanish: \"Hielo Continental\" or \"Campo de Hielo Sur\" ), located at the Southern Patagonic Andes between Chile and Argentina, is the world's second largest contiguous extrapolar ice field. It is the bigger of two remnant parts of the Patagonian Ice Sheet, which covered all of southern Chile during the last glacial period, locally called the Llanquihue glaciation.", "score": 10.9071}], "remaining_searches": 1}
